= Week 4 — Kitchen, Part Two: Cabinets, Gadgets and Containers

Last week you cleared what you can see and what you eat. This week is the clutter behind the doors. Cabinets and drawers are where the waffle maker, the third set of measuring cups and the lids with no containers end up, and because you can't see them, you rarely decide about them.

Here is the test for every tool and gadget: did you use it in the last year? If yes, it stays and goes back where you can reach it. If no, it leaves, unless you only need it once a year and can name the day. Keep the duplicate you like best. Most items this week will be Donate, and a few good pieces may reach your sell threshold from Week 0.

Work one cabinet or drawer a day. Take everything out, wipe the shelf and put back only what passes the test. Don't buy organizers; space usually shows up once the extras are gone.

